ssue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I have an OBJ file with a cube in it where every wall is a named (north, east, south, west, top, bottom). When I open the file in blender, everything is as expected, when I open the file in text editor, there are no noticeable discrepancies between walls, but when I load it with OBJLoader, the file has all the sides (well, at least their naming...) completely mixed up.\n\nSouth is missing (has no children attached to it, therefore mesh cannot be accessed), walls go in order (turning to the right) east, floor, east, north; top is west and bottom is ceiling.\n\nI suspect an issue with OBJLoader, but when I experimented around with it I couldn't find anything standing out.\n\n---\n\nthree.js: r60\ndemo github: https://github.com/uskudnik/obj-not-loading-correctly\n\nControls are implemented, as is raycaster so you can click on a wall and it will write in console what is the name of the object; you can turn with arrow keys, go up/down with arrow keys and move the view around with WSAD.\n","closed_by":{"login":"mrdoob","id":97088,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk3MDg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97088?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob","html_url":"https://github.com/mrdoob","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","si